l</source><volume>38(11)</volume><fpage>895</fpage><lpage>903</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000932-Bernard1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bernard</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>1974</year><article-title>Etude &#x000e9;lectrophysiologique de r&#x000e9;cepteurs impliqu&#x000e9;s dans l'orientation ver l'h&#x000f4;te et dans l'acte h&#x000e9;matophage chez un H&#x000e9;mipt&#x000e8;re : <italic>Triatoma infestans</italic>.</article-title><publisher-loc>France</publisher-loc><fpage>285</fpage><comment>PhD Thesis Universit&#x000e9; de Rennes,</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000932-Catal1"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Catal&#x000e1;</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Sensilla associated with the rostrum of eight species of Triatominae.</article-title><source>J Morphol</source><volume>228</volume><fpage>195</fpage><lpage>201</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8935912</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000932-Sayeed1"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sayeed</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Benzer</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Behavioral genetics of thermosensation and hygrosensation in <italic>Drosophila</italic>.</article-title><source>PNAS</source><volume>93</volume><fpage>6079</fpage><lpage>6084</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8650222</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000932-Zars1"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zars</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Two thermosensors in <italic>Drosophila</italic> have different behavioral functions.</article-title><source>J Comp Physiol A</source><volume>187</volume><fpage>235</fpage><lpage>242</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11401203</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000932-Tracey1"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tracey</surname><given-names>WD</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name><name><surname>Wilson</surname><given-names>RI</given-names></name><name><surname>Laurent</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Benzer</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title><italic>painless</italic>, a <italic>Drosophila</italic> gene essential for nociception.</article-title><source>Cell</source><volume>113</volume><fpage>261</fpage><lpage>273</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12705873</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000932-Xu1"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Xu</surname><given-names>SY</given-names></name><name><surname>Cang</surname><given-names>CL</given-names></name><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>XF</given-names></name><name><surname>Peng</surname><given-names>YQ</given-names></name><name><surname>Ye</surname><given-names>YZ</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Thermal nociception in adult Drosophila: behavioral characterization and the role of the painless gene.</article-title><source>Genes, Brain and Behavior</source><volume>5</volume><fpage>602</fpage><lpage>613</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000932-Reisenman1"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Reisenman</surname><given-names>CE</given-names></name><name><surname>Insausti</surname><given-names>TC</given-names></name><name><surname>Lazzari</surname><given-names>CR</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Light-induced and circadian changes in the compound eye of the haematophagous bug <italic>Triatoma infestans</italic> (Hemiptera: Reduviidae).</article-title><source>J Exp Biol</source><volume>205(2)</volume><fpage>201</fpage><lpage>10</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11821486</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn fn-type="conflict"><p><bold>Competing Interests: </bold>The authors have declared that no competing interests exist.</p></fn><fn fn-type="financial-disclosure"><p><bold>Funding: </bold>Funding was provided by IRR/FIOCRUZ, FAPEMIG, CAPES, CNPq and FAPEBIO/UFMG, CNRS and Universit&#x000e9; Fran&#x000e7;ois Rabelais.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>